Return NULL from gmtime_r() for a time the runtime cannot convert.
gmtime() returns NULL for a time before 1970 or after the year 3000,
and gmtime_r() copied from that pointer without checking it, so it
crashed. httpd crashed this way when it sent the Last-Modified header
of such a file.

Return NULL, as POSIX allows.

---
 win32/mingw.c |    7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1218,7 +1218,12 @@
 struct tm * FAST_FUNC gmtime_r(const time_t *timep, struct tm *result)
 {
 	/* gmtime() in MSVCRT.DLL is thread-safe, but not reentrant */
-	memcpy(result, gmtime(timep), sizeof(struct tm));
+	struct tm *tm = gmtime(timep);
+
+	/* NULL for a time before 1970 or after 3000 */
+	if (tm == NULL)
+		return NULL;
+	memcpy(result, tm, sizeof(struct tm));
 	return result;
 }
 
